# Local development needs no database settings: without DATABASE_URL the app uses an embedded
# Postgres (PGlite) in .pglite/, filled by `npm run db:reset`.
#
# Neon (production) goes into .env.neon, NOT .env – otherwise `npm run dev` would write to it:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://…   (Vercel → teamplaner → Settings → Environment Variables)
# Used only by `npm run db:migrate:neon` and `npm run db:seed:neon`.

# Admin API (Claude, see .claude/skills/teamplaner-admin/SKILL.md): a random token and its SHA-256.
# The server only gets the hash; the token stays with Claude. Same pair in .env.neon for production.
#   ADMIN_TOKEN=…
#   ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH=…

# "Link verloren?": personal links are also stored encrypted with this key (32 random bytes):
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# Never change it in production – stored links become unreadable (they'd be replaced on request).
#   LINK_KEY=…

# Mail through the club's IONOS mailbox. Without SMTP_HOST mails are printed to the console.
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.ionos.de
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=teamplaner@bretten-kangaroos.net
#   SMTP_PASS=…
#   MAIL_FROM=Bretten Kangaroos <teamplaner@bretten-kangaroos.net>

# Daily reminder cron (/api/cron/reminders): Vercel sends this as Bearer token. Without it the cron
# sends nothing – set it only once real families are in the database.
#   CRON_SECRET=…

# Web Push: a key pair, generated once (`npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`). Never change it in
# production – all devices would have to sign up again. Without it everything goes by mail.
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=…
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=…
